Implementing a text editor with multiple list support in Angular involves several steps: setting up the basic structure of your application, creating components for the text area and lists, handling user input, and styling it properly. Below is a step-by-step guide to help you get started:

### Step 1: Set Up Your Angular Project

First, make sure you have Angular CLI installed. If not, install it using npm or yarn.

```bash
npm install -g @angular/cli
```

Then, create a new Angular project if you haven't already done so.

```bash
ng new my-text-editor-app
cd my-text-editor-app
```

### Step 2: Create Components

Create the main component where the text editor will reside.

```bash
ng generate component text-editor
```

This command generates an `app.component.html`, `app.component.css`, and `app.component.ts` files. Modify these files as follows:

#### app.component.html
```html
<div>
  <h1>Text Editor</h1>
  <textarea #editor></textarea>
  <ul *ngFor="let item of items">
    <li>{{item}}</li>
  </ul>
</div>
```

